          "quote": "9.4 Customer may terminate this Agreement or any Order Form without cause by delivering the written notice specified in Section 29.4. Customer owes only accrued Fees, and Vendor shall refund prepaid Fees for the period after termination.",
          "rationale": "Section 9.4 gives Customer an unconditional without-cause right to terminate the Agreement or any Order Form, and Section 29.4 fixes that notice period at thirty days before the effective termination date — at or better than the preferred 30-day standard. Customer owes only accrued Fees and Vendor must refund prepaid Fees for the post-termination period (echoed in Section 10.2 for prepaid recurring Fees), with no early-termination fee, unwind charge, or penalty anywhere in Sections 7, 9, 10 or 11 (Section 7.7's liquidated damages are triggered only by late payment, a separate rule). On the Vendor side, Section 9's only Vendor termination triggers are material breach (9.1) and insolvency (9.2); Vendor is given no convenience right at all during the three-year term (Section 8.1), and under Section 8.2 even non-renewal of an Order Form is a Customer-only election, so this comfortably exceeds the fallback (which would tolerate Vendor convenience termination at term end on 90 days' notice). Two points to note without redlining: \"Fees\" is defined narrowly in Section 1.5 as the Implementation Fee, so the preferred pro-rata refund of prepaid subscription amounts is weaker than the label suggests, and 9.4 does not spell out \"in whole or in part\". Neither is required by the fallback checklist, so this sits above the fallback and is not redlined here.",
